Headless engine mode: Kodi sees the real display.

With KODI_ENGINE_MODE set, Kodi's window is a Dialog window that is never attached, so its decor
view has no Display: Kodi saw no HDR capabilities, no display modes and a 60 Hz refresh rate.
CAndroidUtils now falls back to the default display (WindowManager.getDefaultDisplay()) for HDR
capabilities, display modes and the refresh rate. The display mode belongs to the window of the
host application: in engine mode CXBMCApp::SetDisplayMode() and SetRefreshRate() only log (Kodi
used to wait 5 s at startup for a display change that never came), and the only resolution Kodi
offers is the current display mode at the size of the Surface it renders to (see 0001).

